\begin_layout Standard
The final considerations are the geometry of the lamella and the protective
 layers used to preserve the region of interest (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:FIB_lamella_planning"

\end_inset

).
 In this work, coatings of 10 nm amorphous carbon followed by 3 nm of Au/Pd
 were applied to the whole surface using a specimen coater.
 In the FIB, site specific coatings of platinum were applied using the electron
 and ion beams to protect the underlying specimen
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "haigh2012crosssectional"

\end_inset

.
 During the final steps of ion beam polishing, the beam was angled so that
 the top of the lamella (≡ specimen surface) became tapered to form a wedge.
 A full description of the sample preparation is given next in section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:FIB-preparation-of"

\end_inset

.
